ge><lpage>68</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/lsm.10113</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">T. Krueger, H. J. Altermatt, D. Mettler, B. Scholl, L. Magnusson, and H. B. Ris. Experimental photodynamic therapy for malignant pleural mesothelioma with pegylated mTHPC. Lasers Surg. Med. 32:61&#x02013;68 (2003). <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12516073</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reuther</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubler</surname><given-names>A. C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zillmann</surname><given-names>U.</given-names></name><name><surname>Flechtenmacher</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinn</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of the <italic>in vivo</italic> efficiency of photofrin II-, mTHPC-, mTHPC-PEG- and mTHPCnPEG-mediated PDT in a human xenografted head and neck carcinoma</article-title><source>Lasers Surg. Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>314</fpage><lpage>322</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/lsm.1123</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">T. Reuther, A. C. Kubler, U. Zillmann, C. Flechtenmacher, and H. Sinn. Comparison of the in vivo efficiency of photofrin II-, mTHPC-, mTHPC-PEG- and mTHPCnPEG-mediated PDT in a human xenografted head and neck carcinoma. Lasers Surg. Med. 29:314&#x02013;322 (2001). <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11746108</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grahn</surname><given-names>M. F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Giger</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>McGuinness</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jode</surname><given-names>M. L.</given-names></name><name><